0 1 0 0 0 0 2 1\n0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 2 0\n0 0 0 0 0 2 0 0 2 0\n0 0 2 0 0 2 0 0 2 0\n0 0 2 0 2 2 0 0 2 0\n0 0 2 0 2 2 2 0 2 0\n\nYour final answer should just be the python script itself, no other text or markdown.",
  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0]) if h else 0\n\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    # Remove original 2s\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            if out[r][c] == 2:\n                out[r][c] = 0\n\n    # For each column, move the column's 2-count upward into the first\n    # zero-run that appears after the top 1-segment.\n    for c in range(w):\n        count2 = sum(1 for r in range(h) if grid[r][c] == 2)\n        if count2 == 0:\n            continue\n\n        seen_one = False\n        start = None\n        for r in range(h):\n            if grid[r][c] == 1:\n                seen_one = True\n            elif seen_one and out[r][c] == 0:\n                start = r\n                break\n\n        if start is None:\n            continue\n\n        placed = 0\n        r = start\n        while r < h and placed < count2:\n            if out[r][c] == 0:\n                out[r][c] = 2\n                placed += 1\n            r += 1\n\n    return out",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0]) if h else 0\n\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    # Remove original 2s\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            if out[r][c] == 2:\n                out[r][c] = 0\n\n    # For each column, move the column's 2-count upward into the first\n    # zero-run that appears after the top 1-segment.\n    for c in range(w):\n        count2 = sum(1 for r in range(h) if grid[r][c] == 2)\n        if count2 == 0:\n            continue\n\n        seen_one = False\n        start = None\n        for r in range(h):\n            if grid[r][c] == 1:\n                seen_one = True\n            elif seen_one and out[r][c] == 0:\n                start = r\n                break\n\n        if start is None:\n            continue\n\n        placed = 0\n        r = start\n        while r < h and placed < count2:\n            if out[r][c] == 0:\n                out[r][c] = 2\n                placed += 1\n            r += 1\n\n    return out",
